WEBVTT

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.740
<b>Ikebukuro Sweets Special!</b>

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:36.220
Aoi?

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.880
<i>Hinata?</i>

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.360
<i>Do you want something?</i>

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.400
I'm calling you because I want something.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.920
You're free tomorrow, aren't you?

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.500
Let's go hang out in Ikebukuro.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:48.620
<i>We should check out the 
planetarium at Sunshine City.</i>

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.210
<i>There's a popular VR thing, too.</i>

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.630
VR? What's that?

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:53.500
<i>Dunno.</i>

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.940
<i>The crêpe shop Mio told me 
about looks really good.</i>

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:00.160
<i>I heard the line-up is, like, an hour long—</i>

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.170
Actually, I can't tomorrow.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:01.900
<i>What?!</i>

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:02.920
Why not?

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:03.730
<i>Work.</i>

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:04.720
The day after?

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.390
<i>I'm working the day after, too.</i>

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:10.210
Sorry, but you'll have to go on your own.

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:13.400
Well, I have to get up 
early tomorrow. Goodnight.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.400
Aoi!

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:18.150
Bah, lame.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.970
I did a ton of research for nothing.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:26.410
<b>She Who Does Not Work, 
Neither Shall She Climb?!</b>

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.420
<b>Hanasaika
Susuki</b>

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.840
Strawberry shortcake...

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.000
Mont Blanc...

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.170
<b>Today's Special</b>

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.170
<b>Candied Chestnut Pie</b>

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.300
And next to that goes the Eierschecke.

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:38.250
I wonder why this cheesecake 
is called Eierschecke.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:39.430
What language is that, anyway?

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:40.920
Gutefrage!

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.580
Good question.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:43.540
Hikari-san.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.190
That's German.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.810
It's a snack from Dresden, 
in eastern Germany.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.270
"Eier" is "egg," and "schecke" means "dapple."

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:55.030
The name comes from the dapple pattern 
on the surface when it's baked.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.030
You know a lot.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.460
Danke schön!

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:00.470
I'm taking a German class at my university.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.610
Wow!

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.050
I've been working here for three years.

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:05.080
Ask me anything about cake.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.080
Then, what does Mont Blanc mean?

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:09.580
That, I don't know.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.490
Come on...

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.580
It's the name of a mountain.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:18.590
The name Mont Blanc comes from 
the highest mountain in the Alps.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:21.490
The shape represents the treacherous ridges,

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:24.730
the thin-striped cream represents 
the sharp rock faces,

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:29.070
and powdered sugar represents 
the beautiful white snow.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.600
Oh!

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:34.530
It's a mountain cake, enjoyed 
by the name "white mountain."

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:35.610
White mountain?

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:39.610
Mont Blanc is French for "white mountain."

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.450
That's our manager!

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.840
Ask me anything about cake.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:49.240
All right, it's almost time to open.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.970
I'm counting on you.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:51.830
Okay!

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:01.630
Is that Mt. Fuji?

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.240
Hey, look, Aoi! It's Mt...

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:11.730
<i>Shoot, force of habit.</i>

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.930
Thank you very much.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:39.590
You look so proper, Aoi-chan.

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:40.380
Huh?

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.470
You seem totally different 
from when you're at school.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.240
You look a lot more dependable than usual.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:48.540
And Yuri is as indecisive as ever.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:51.720
Well, they all look so good. I can't decide!

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.100
Fine, fine, I get it.

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:57.100
<i>"More than usual"?</i>

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:59.960
<i>Do I seem</i> that <i>undependable at school?</i>

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:02.380
You're so dependable, Aoi-chan.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:04.280
Please don't make fun of me.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:07.310
No, your friend's right.

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:09.460
You work much faster now, too.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:11.950
Yeah! I feel comfortable seeing you work now.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.820
U-Um...

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.690
Thank you.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:18.540
<i>Oh...</i>

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:21.680
<i>I guess I'm doing a good job.</i>

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.860
Isn't it amazing, Aoi—

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.580
<i>I did it again.</i>

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:41.320
Aoi-chan!

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.940
Eierschecke long, please!

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.560
You look happy, Kaede-san.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:50.720
Yeah! Yuka's out on a family 
vacation today and tomorrow.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.700
I don't have to be forced to study.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.450
What freedom!

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:59.720
I feel so unshackled, 
like I could scale the Alps.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.960
Freedom is so great!

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:06.800
10,000 feet of the Alps, 
big dreams, small dreams!

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:07.070
<i>She must have been really stressed out.</i>

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.970
Alpen dancing up Mt. Fuji!

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:09.430
<i>Studying for exams is scary.</i>

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:11.100
Hey!

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.540
I'm here.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.560
Okay, I'm taking a picture.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.940
What is this? It's so cute.

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:43.220
Let's see... local toy?

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:46.150
And it serves as a good-luck charm! Wow!

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.800
<b>Mt. Akagi</b>

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.800
<b>Fall Leaves and Hot Springs</b>

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:53.800
Thank you.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:02.560
Are you okay?

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.690
Can you stand?

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:09.740
You didn't cry. What a big girl.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:10.950
Are you shopping by yourself?

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:13.920
I'm a big sister now.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.470
I can do it myself.

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:16.820
A big sister?

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:17.700
Yeah.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:20.710
I just got a new little sister.

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:23.230
Mom's coming home today

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:27.510
from the hospital, so I wanted 
to buy her favorite cake.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:29.520
Wow, what a good big sister!

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:30.860
That's wonderful.

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:32.980
I'm sure your mom will be happy.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:34.980
Uh-huh!

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:39.480
Soufflé au fromage

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.480
One soufflé au fromage, please.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.440
Coming right up.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.770
I saved up my allowance 
and shopping money.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.140
That's amazing.

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:52.510
Let's see, you have 399 yen in all.

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:54.160
Uh-huh! Just enough!

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:56.440
399 yen!

00:07:57.220 --> 00:07:58.860
Just enough.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.790
Soufflé au fromage
399 yen (plus tax)

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:04.290
<i>Taxes...</i>

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.860
Um... ah...

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:09.720
Hey...

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:12.300
That's 399 yen.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:14.480
Thank you very much.

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:16.090
Prepare it, please.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:16.930
Okay.

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:21.930
She chose our cake for her 
family's special occasion.

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:24.440
She's an important customer.

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.940
It's a special service, just for today.

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:32.490
<i>That's right.</i>

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:38.390
<i>People put all kinds of wishes into their 
gifts, even if it's just a slice of cake.</i>

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:40.200
<i>All right!</i>

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:43.690
<i>I have to work even harder!</i>

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.530
<b>Today's Special</b>

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.530
<b>Candied Chestnut Pie</b>

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.530
<b>325 yen</b>

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.490
Let's see...

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:54.090
<b>Horned Owl</b>

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:54.090
Is Aoi working hard?

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:55.840
There she is.

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:05.020
She's actually doing a good job.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.450
<i>I guess I'll give this to her next time.</i>

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.740
Thank you.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:20.070
That's it for the day.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:23.870
I didn't make it!

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:27.710
I promised I'd buy one today.

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:32.440
I'm going to disappoint my daughter again.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:36.270
I guess I'll buy a cake 
at the convenience store.

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:38.340
U-Um...

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:43.970
We don't have many left, but...

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:44.900
That's fine!

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:47.310
Thank you! Thank you!

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.830
Do you have any shortcakes left?

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:52.970
Sorry, we're all out for the day.

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:56.240
I see... What should I do?

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:58.900
What else might she like?

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:00.620
What does she like?

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:02.370
She likes mountain climbing.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:03.840
Mountain climbing?

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:06.620
Sorry! You're talking about cakes, of course.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:10.410
What does she like, other than shortcakes?

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:12.400
How about a Mont Blanc, then?

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.630
Mont Blanc?

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:17.210
It's named after a mountain in the Alps.

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:20.000
The cream is shaped like a mountain,

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.920
and there's powdered sugar on 
top to make it look like snow.

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:25.440
Oh, really?

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:29.070
Mont Blanc is German for "white mountain."

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:31.150
No, I mean, uh...

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:32.600
It's French.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:34.150
Right.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:38.150
It's a mountain-themed cake 
that has that French name.

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:40.020
A mountain-themed cake?

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:43.780
I bet she would love that.

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:45.880
May I have two, then?

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:48.750
Thank you.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:54.420
<i>She wanted someone important 
to her to be happy.</i>

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:58.740
<i>And we help with those wishes.</i>

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:02.290
<i>I wonder if I managed to do that.</i>

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:10.710
Cake from Susuki!

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:14.010
It's a mountain-themed cake that 
the shop staff recommended.

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:15.840
A mountain-themed cake?

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:17.110
What's that?

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:18.990
Open it.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:19.840
Okay.

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:24.870
It's a Mont Blanc! It looks delicious!

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:26.490
Right?

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:31.020
Apparently, Mont Blanc is the 
name of a mountain in the Alps.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:33.440
Oh! So that's what makes it mountain-themed?

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:34.500
Yeah!

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:41.010
<b>Mt. Akagi</b>

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:39.090
Mt. Akagi.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.010
Maybe we'll go here next.

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:43.950
Aoi could handle this one easily.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:59.940
<b>Honoka-chan</b>

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:59.940
<b>To Be Continued</b>
